## c1-px1 | Calc 1 exam practice: limits and derivatives | maths | 1 | calc1 | c1-rules
quiz 2 | lim x→2 (x² − 4)/(x − 2) = ?
* 4
o 0
o 2
o Undefined
= Factor: (x − 2)(x + 2)/(x − 2) = x + 2 → 4.
> Next problem

quiz 2 | lim x→0 sin(5x)/x = ?
* 5
o 1
o 0
o 1/5
= sin(5x)/x = 5 · sin(5x)/(5x) → 5.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | lim x→∞ (3x² − x)/(1 − 2x²) = ?
* −3/2
o 3/2
o 0
o −∞
= Ratio of leading coefficients: 3/(−2).
> Next problem

quiz 2 | d/dx (x³ + 2x)⁴ = ?
* 4(x³ + 2x)³(3x² + 2)
o 4(x³ + 2x)³
o (3x² + 2)⁴
o 4(3x² + 2)³
= Chain rule: outer 4(·)³, inner 3x² + 2.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | d/dx (eˣ cos x) = ?
* eˣ(cos x − sin x)
o −eˣ sin x
o eˣ(cos x + sin x)
o eˣ cos x
= Product rule: eˣ cos x + eˣ(−sin x).
> Next problem

quiz 3 | d/dx ln(cos x) = ?
* −tan x
o 1/cos x
o tan x
o −1/sin x
= (1/cos x)(−sin x).
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Equation of the tangent to y = x² at x = 3?
* y = 6x − 9
o y = 6x + 9
o y = 3x
o y = 9x − 18
= Slope 6 at (3, 9): y − 9 = 6(x − 3).
> Next problem

quiz 3 | d/dx (x/(x² + 1)) = ?
* (1 − x²)/(x² + 1)²
o 1/(2x)
o (x² − 1)/(x² + 1)²
o 1/(x² + 1)
= Quotient rule: ((x² + 1) − 2x²)/(x² + 1)².
> Next problem

quiz 4 | f(x) = x³ − 12x. On [−3, 3], what's the absolute maximum?
* 16
o 9
o 0
o 27
= Critical points x = ±2: f(−2) = 16, f(2) = −16. Endpoints: f(−3) = 9, f(3) = −9.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | d/dx arcsin(2x) = ?
* 2/√(1 − 4x²)
o 1/√(1 − 4x²)
o 2/√(1 − x²)
o 1/(1 + 4x²)
= Chain rule on 1/√(1 − u²) with u = 2x.
> Next set: integrals

## c1-px2 | Calc 1 exam practice: integrals | maths | 1 | calc1 | c1-sub
quiz 2 | ∫ (1/x) dx from 1 to e = ?
* 1
o e
o 0
o e − 1
= ln e − ln 1 = 1.
> Next problem

quiz 2 | ∫ cos(3x) dx = ?
* (1/3) sin(3x) + C
o 3 sin(3x) + C
o −(1/3) sin(3x) + C
o sin(3x) + C
= Reverse chain rule: divide by the inner derivative.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫₀¹ (2x + 1)⁴ dx = ?
* 24.2
o 121
o 12.1
o 48.4
= u = 2x + 1: (1/2)∫₁³ u⁴ du = (1/10)(243 − 1) = 24.2.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫ x/(x² + 4) dx = ?
* ½ ln(x² + 4) + C
o ln(x² + 4) + C
o ½ arctan(x/2) + C
o 2 ln(x² + 4) + C
= u = x² + 4, du = 2x dx.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫ 1/(x² + 9) dx = ?
* (1/3) arctan(x/3) + C
o arctan(x/3) + C
o (1/9) arctan(x) + C
o ln(x² + 9) + C
= Standard form ∫ 1/(x² + a²) = (1/a) arctan(x/a).
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Area between y = √x and y = x from 0 to 1?
* 1/6
o 1/3
o 1/2
o 2/3
= √x is above: ∫₀¹ (√x − x) dx = 2/3 − 1/2.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Volume when y = x (0 ≤ x ≤ 2) spins about the x-axis?
* 8π/3
o 2π
o 4π
o 8π
= π∫₀² x² dx = 8π/3: a cone.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | ∫₋₁¹ x³cos(x) dx = ?
* 0
o 2 sin 1
o 1
o π
= x³cos x is odd. Symmetric limits.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | A particle has v(t) = 3t² − 6t. Displacement from t = 0 to t = 3?
* 0
o 27
o 9
o −4
= ∫₀³ (3t² − 6t) dt = [t³ − 3t²]₀³ = 27 − 27 = 0.
= Back where it started, though it travelled a distance of 8.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | d/dx ∫ₓ^(x²) sin t dt = ?
* 2x sin(x²) − sin x
o sin(x²) − sin x
o 2x sin(x²)
o cos(x²) − cos x
= FTC with both limits variable: upper limit term minus lower limit term.
> Calc 2 practice next

## c2-px1 | Calc 2 exam practice: techniques | maths | 1 | calc2 | c2-trigsub
quiz 3 | ∫ x ln x dx = ?
* (x²/2) ln x − x²/4 + C
o x ln x − x + C
o (x²/2) ln x + C
o ln x/2 + C
= u = ln x, dv = x dx.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫ sin²x cos x dx = ?
* (1/3) sin³x + C
o (1/3) cos³x + C
o sin x cos x + C
o −(1/3) sin³x + C
= u = sin x.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | ∫ 1/(x(x + 1)) dx = ?
* ln|x/(x + 1)| + C
o ln|x(x + 1)| + C
o 1/(x + 1) + C
o ln|x + 1| − 1/x + C
= Partial fractions: 1/x − 1/(x + 1).
> Next problem

quiz 4 | ∫ dx/√(4 − x²) = ?
* arcsin(x/2) + C
o arccos(2x) + C
o (1/2) arcsin x + C
o ln|x + √(4 − x²)| + C
= x = 2 sin θ turns it into ∫ dθ.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫₀^∞ e^(−2x) dx = ?
* 1/2
o 2
o ∞
o 1
= [−½e^(−2x)]₀^∞ = 0 + ½.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | ∫₀^∞ x e^(−x) dx = ?
* 1
o 0
o ∞
o 1/2
= Parts, or Γ(2) = 1! = 1.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∫ sec²x tan x dx = ?
* ½ tan²x + C
o tan x + C
o sec x + C
o ½ sec x + C
= u = tan x, du = sec²x dx.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Does ∫₁^∞ 1/x^1.01 dx converge?
* Yes
o No
o Only conditionally
= p = 1.01 > 1. It converges (to 100), just barely.
> Series practice next

## c2-px2 | Calc 2 exam practice: series | maths | 2 | calc2 | c2-tests
quiz 3 | Does Σ n/(n² + 1) converge?
* No
o Yes
o Only absolutely
= Limit comparison with 1/n, which diverges.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Does Σ 1/2ⁿ · n converge? (Σ n/2ⁿ)
* Yes, to 2
o No
o Yes, to 1
o Yes, to 4
= Ratio test gives 1/2 < 1. The exact sum is 2.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Radius of convergence of Σ (x − 3)ⁿ/(n·4ⁿ)?
* 4
o 3
o 1/4
o 1
= Ratio test: |x − 3|/4 < 1.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Maclaurin series of 1/(1 + x²) starts…
* 1 − x² + x⁴ − x⁶ + …
o 1 + x² + x⁴ + …
o x − x³/3 + …
o 1 − x + x² − …
= Geometric series with ratio −x².
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Σ from n=0 to ∞ of xⁿ/n! evaluated at x = ln 3?
* 3
o ln 3
o e³
o 1/3
= That's e^x at x = ln 3.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Σ from n=1 to ∞ of 1/(n(n + 1)) = ?
* 1
o ∞
o 1/2
o 2
= Telescoping: 1/n − 1/(n + 1). Everything cancels except the first 1.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Taylor series of cos x about 0: the coefficient of x⁴?
* 1/24
o −1/24
o 1/4
o 1/12
= cos x = 1 − x²/2 + x⁴/24 − …
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Which test settles Σ (−1)ⁿ/ln(n) for n ≥ 2?
* Alternating series test (converges)
o Ratio test
o Divergence test (diverges)
o p-test
= 1/ln n decreases to 0. It converges, but not absolutely.
> Calc 3 practice next

## c3-px1 | Calc 3 exam practice | maths | 2 | calc3 | c3-cs
quiz 3 | f(x, y) = e^(xy). f_x = ?
* y e^(xy)
o x e^(xy)
o e^(xy)
o xy e^(xy)
= Treat y as a constant.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∇(x² + y² + z²) at (1, −1, 2)?
* (2, −2, 4)
o (1, −1, 2)
o (2, 2, 4)
o 6
= ∇ = (2x, 2y, 2z).
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Critical point of f = x² + xy + y² − 3x?
* (2, −1)
o (1, −1)
o (3, 0)
o (0, 0)
= f_x = 2x + y − 3 = 0, f_y = x + 2y = 0 → x = 2, y = −1.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | ∬ over [0,1]×[0,2] of xy dA = ?
* 1
o 2
o 1/2
o 4
= (∫₀¹ x dx)(∫₀² y dy) = (1/2)(2) = 1.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | div of F = (x², yz, z²)?
* 2x + 3z
o 2x + y + 2z
o (2x, z, 2z)
o x² + yz + z²
= ∂(x²)/∂x + ∂(yz)/∂y + ∂(z²)/∂z = 2x + z + 2z = 2x + 3z.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | curl of F = (y, −x, 0)?
* (0, 0, −2)
o (0, 0, 2)
o (0, 0, 0)
o (1, −1, 0)
= z-component: ∂(−x)/∂x − ∂y/∂y = −1 − 1 = −2.
= It rotates clockwise.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | ∮ (x dy − y dx) around the unit circle = ?
* 2π
o π
o 0
o 4π
= Green: ∬ (1 + 1) dA = 2 × π. In general ½∮(x dy − y dx) is the enclosed area.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Volume of the region under z = 4 − x² − y² and above z = 0?
* 8π
o 4π
o 16π
o 32π/3
= Polar: ∫₀^2π ∫₀² (4 − r²) r dr dθ = 2π(8 − 4) = 8π.
> Next problem

quiz 3 | Work by F = (2x, 2y) along any path from (0,0) to (1,2)?
* 5
o 3
o 2
o Depends on the path
= F = ∇(x² + y²). Work = φ(1,2) − φ(0,0) = 5.
> Next problem

quiz 4 | Flux of F = (x, y, z) through the closed unit cube [0,1]³?
* 3
o 1
o 6
o 0
= Divergence theorem: div F = 3 times volume 1.
> All calculus practice sets done
